| pp. 105-106                | Need to choose network structure and parameters               | Separate motivation from claims of universal superiority                   |
| Section 4.1.1, pp. 106-108 | Growth, pruning, connection, and interface mutations          | Immutable DAG edits; identity splice with a precise preservation condition |
| Section 4.1.2, pp. 108-113 | Sequence genes and DXNN-style node tuples                     | One canonical edge map; derived per-node views                             |
| Section 4.1.3, pp. 113-118 | Direct and indirect mapping; [3,5,2] substrate                | Batch graph interpreter and one-neuron coordinate generator                |
| Section 4.2.1, pp. 118-122 | XOR scape, reciprocal error, mutation-based evolution         | Rounded cosine audit; finite error-based selection; bounded masked TWEANN  |
| Section 4.2.2, pp. 123-127 | Double-pole task and interfaces                               | Contract tests, not an invented physical simulator                         |
| Section 4.2.3, pp. 127-135 | Modular morphology, shared ecology, bootstrapped reproduction | Research proposal retained; isolated resource-accounting demonstration     |
| Section 4.3, pp. 135-137   | Topology search plus local weight tuning; spawning pools      | Counted local/independent trials and explicit inheritance choice           |
| Section 4.4, pp. 138-140   | Neuroevolution as specialized graph-based GP                  | Shared interpreter perspective with declared execution limits              |
| Section 4.5, pp. 140-141   | Source bibliography                                           | Selected reading pointers, without claiming independent review             |

