### Validation note

Independent Python/NumPy reference implementations passed **39 algorithmic
checks**, and **7 notebook-structure checks** also passed. These cover graph
mutations, scalar/batched parity, substrate shapes, the cosine audit, masked
variation, elite preservation, evaluation budgets, pole-interface boundaries,
reproduction accounting, and local-search invariants.

The reference random generator is **not Nx.Random**, so its stochastic traces
are not claimed to reproduce the notebook's seed exactly. The authoring
environment has no Elixir/Erlang runtime: **the actual Elixir/Nx cells and
Livebook visual rendering have not been executed here**. The notebook includes
**30 executable assertions** to run in your own runtime. Those assertions do
not require a lucky stochastic search outcome.

**End of Chapter 4.**
